From: Tilo <noreply@tilo.so>
Subject: [PATCH] oci: store a layer's objects in parallel

Draining a layer stored its objects one at a time: each a copy into the
repository and an fs-verity enable, which first writes the file out. A
repo-to-repo copy across filesystems (`cfsctl oci copy`, an install from the
booted repository) spent most of its time waiting on those writes in turn.
A few worker threads now store objects while the stream is read on, and the
splitstream is still written in stream order, each reference once its object
is stored.
